 #. (itstool) path: sect2/title
 #: C/gnumeric.xml:136
 msgid "The complexities of text format files"
-msgstr ""
+msgstr "Textfilernas komplexitet"
 
 #. (itstool) path: sect2/para
 #: C/gnumeric.xml:138
 msgid ""
 "The use of text format files to store and transmit data for use in a "
 "spreadsheet involves three somewhat complex decisions which determine how "
-"the file expresses and separates each data value. These complexities must be "
-"understood for a user to be able to use the <interface>Text Import</"
-"interface> druid effectively. These complexities exist because of the "
-"limitations of early computers and because or the historical development of "
-"computer systems by different manufacturers and programmers, in different "
-"countries, targeting different types of users, speaking different languages."
-msgstr ""
+"the file expresses and separates each data value. These complexities must be"
+" understood for a user to be able to use the <interface>Text "
+"Import</interface> druid effectively. These complexities exist because of "
+"the limitations of early computers and because or the historical development"
+" of computer systems by different manufacturers and programmers, in "
+"different countries, targeting different types of users, speaking different "
+"languages."
+msgstr ""
+"När textfiler används för att lagra och överföra data till kalkylblad "
+"behöver tre ganska komplicerade val göras. De avgör hur varje datavärde "
+"skrivs och avgränsas. Du behöver förstå dessa delar för att kunna använda "
+"guiden <interface>Textimport</interface> effektivt. Komplexiteten beror dels"
+" på begränsningarna hos tidiga datorer, dels på att datorsystem har "
+"utvecklats på olika sätt av olika tillverkare och programmerare, i olika "
+"länder och för användare med olika språk."
 
 #. (itstool) path: sect2/para
 #: C/gnumeric.xml:151
@@ -33936,15 +43058,23 @@
 "The first complexity involves the different systems which relate the "
 "contents of a computer file to the characters in a written language. All "
 "text files on a computer consist of a long sequence of binary digits. Text "
-"files are files in which these digits are used to indicate different textual "
-"characters. Character 'encodings' are standardized systems which relate the "
-"binary digits in a computer file to a formal system of characters which "
+"files are files in which these digits are used to indicate different textual"
+" characters. Character 'encodings' are standardized systems which relate the"
+" binary digits in a computer file to a formal system of characters which "
 "includes both text glyphs (shapes) and formatting indicators. Each encoding "
 "defines a way to interpret the binary digits and uses the characters from a "
 "particular character set. The alternative character encoding strategies are "
 "explained in greater detail in <xref linkend=\"sect-file-textImport-complex-"
 "encoding\"/>, below."
 msgstr ""
+"Den första utmaningen är hur olika system kopplar innehållet i en datorfil "
+"till tecknen i ett skriftspråk. Alla textfiler består av långa följder av "
+"binära siffror, som används för att representera olika tecken. "
+"Teckenkodningar är standardiserade system som kopplar siffrorna i filen till"
+" en formell teckenuppsättning med både texttecken och formateringstecken. "
+"Varje kodning anger hur siffrorna ska tolkas och bygger på en viss "
+"teckenuppsättning. Olika sätt att koda tecken förklaras närmare i <xref "
+"linkend=\"sect-file-textImport-complex-encoding\"/> nedan."
 
 #. (itstool) path: sect2/para
 #: C/gnumeric.xml:167
@@ -33958,112 +43088,160 @@
 "explained in greater detail in <xref linkend=\"sect-file-textImport-complex-"
 "lineBreak\"/>, below."
 msgstr ""
+"Den andra utmaningen är hur filens tecken delas upp i rader. I textfiler "
+"markeras slutet på varje rad med ett visst tecken eller en teckensekvens. "
+"Olika datorsystem använder olika tecken för detta. Alternativen för "
+"radbrytning beskrivs närmare i <xref linkend=\"sect-file-textImport-complex-"
+"lineBreak\"/> nedan."
 
 #. (itstool) path: sect2/para
 #: C/gnumeric.xml:179
 msgid ""
-"The third complexity involves the decision of how to separate the characters "
-"in each line into separate value fields. Again, different strategies exist. "
-"These can be separated into two broad categories: strategies which use a "
+"The third complexity involves the decision of how to separate the characters"
+" in each line into separate value fields. Again, different strategies exist."
+" These can be separated into two broad categories: strategies which use a "
 "character or sequence of characters to separate the values, so called "
-"'delimited' or 'separated' strategies, and strategies which use the position "
-"of the character in the line to separate the values, so called 'fixed-width' "
-"strategies. The alternative data structuring strategies are explained in "
-"greater detail in <xref linkend=\"sect-file-textImport-complex-dataStruct\"/"
-">, below."
-msgstr ""
+"'delimited' or 'separated' strategies, and strategies which use the position"
+" of the character in the line to separate the values, so called 'fixed-"
+"width' strategies. The alternative data structuring strategies are explained"
+" in greater detail in <xref linkend=\"sect-file-textImport-complex-"
+"dataStruct\"/>, below."
+msgstr ""
+"Den tredje utmaningen är hur tecknen på varje rad delas upp i olika "
+"värdefält. Det finns två huvudmetoder: avgränsade värden, där ett tecken "
+"eller en teckensekvens skiljer värdena åt, och värden med fast bredd, där "
+"tecknens position på raden avgör var värdena börjar och slutar. Metoderna "
+"beskrivs närmare i <xref linkend=\"sect-file-textImport-complex-"
+"dataStruct\"/> nedan."
 
 #. (itstool) path: sect2/para
 #: C/gnumeric.xml:193
 msgid ""
-"Fortunately, the <application>Gnumeric</application> <interface>Text Import</"
-"interface> druid provides users with a way to preview the information in a "
-"text file. This enables users to change the settings which determine each of "
-"these three conventions until the text in the preview correctly shows the "
-"contents of the data file. Therefore, while the details of these three steps "
-"are complex, the practical impact on users is minimal. Users can simply "
-"experiment until the file appears correct without having to understand each "
-"of these complexities in detail."
-msgstr ""
+"Fortunately, the <application>Gnumeric</application> <interface>Text "
+"Import</interface> druid provides users with a way to preview the "
+"information in a text file. This enables users to change the settings which "
